@*
    Shared ALTERNATIVE-EMAIL banner — surfaced at the top of every role's task
    page so the secondary-email option isn't buried in My Hub Profile.

    TASK reminders are CC'd to the RESOLVED alternate address
    (AlternateEmailPolicy.CcFor: organizer-set SecondaryEmail first, then the
    participant's own AlternateEmail) — see ParticipantEmailService.ResolveRouting
    and TaskReminderBuilder. This banner tells the person which inbox(es) those
    reminders reach and lets them add or change the alternative inbox in one tap.

    §660 — CALENDAR INVITES ARE NOT CC'd, and this comment used to say they were.
    CalendarInviteEmailService resolves ONE address (SpeakerProfile.CalendarEmailFor)
    and calls IEmailSender.SendWithIcsAsync, which has no cc parameter. Before
    claiming a mail family is copied anywhere, check that its send site passes a cc —
    only TaskReminderBuilder and the shared ParticipantEmailService seam do.

    §422 fixed two faults here (operator 2026-07-27: "it appears as the alternative
    email didn't pick up here as well, as it still shows primary email here"):

      1. It read ONLY SecondaryEmail, which no participant-facing screen can set —
         it is organizer-only. So someone who added their alternate address on their
         own profile saw this banner keep insisting they had just one inbox.
      2. The link pointed at /Profile#SecondaryEmail, an anchor that does not exist
         on that page. The box they actually landed next to was AlternateEmail.

    Together those made the banner advertise something it could not deliver: it
    invited you to add an address, and then ignored the one you added.

    Self-contained: reads the CURRENT participant (honours organizer "act as")
    and looks up their secondary email, so it drops into any page with one line:
        @await Html.PartialAsync("Shared/_SecondaryEmailBanner")
*@
@using CommunityHub.Auth
@using CommunityHub.Core.Data
@using CommunityHub.Core.Domain
@using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore
@inject ICurrentParticipantAccessor CurrentParticipant
@inject CommunityHubDbContext Db
@{
    var me = CurrentParticipant.Current;
    string primary = me?.Email ?? string.Empty;
    string? secondary = null;
    // §660 — the CALENDAR address, resolved exactly as CalendarInviteEmailService resolves it.
    string? calendarInbox = null;
    if (me is not null)
    {
        var row = await Db.Participants
            .Where(p => p.Id == me.ParticipantId)
            .Select(p => new { p.SecondaryEmail, p.AlternateEmail })
            .FirstOrDefaultAsync();
        secondary = CommunityHub.Core.Participants.AlternateEmailPolicy.CcFor(
            row?.SecondaryEmail, row?.AlternateEmail);

        var sp = await Db.SpeakerProfiles
            .Where(x => x.ParticipantId == me.ParticipantId)
            .Select(x => new { x.CalendarEmail, x.ContactEmailOverride })
            .FirstOrDefaultAsync();
        calendarInbox = SpeakerProfile.CalendarEmailFor(
            primary, sp?.CalendarEmail, sp?.ContactEmailOverride);
    }
    var hasSecondary = !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(secondary);
    // Only worth calling out when the calendar invite lands somewhere OTHER than the primary.
    var calendarDiffers = !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(calendarInbox)
        && !string.Equals(calendarInbox, primary, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
}
@if (me is not null)
{
    <div class="alt-email-banner"
         style="margin:0 0 16px;padding:12px 14px;border-radius:8px;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.55;
                background:@(hasSecondary ? "#f0fdf4" : "#eff6ff");
                border:1px solid @(hasSecondary ? "#bbf7d0" : "#bfdbfe");
                border-left:4px solid @(hasSecondary ? "#16a34a" : "#2563eb");color:#1f2937;">
        @* §660 (operator 2026-07-29: "i dont believe it is true that mails go to both primary and
           alternative mail, which mails this text wrong"). He was right, and the banner was wrong
           in a specific way worth remembering: it said "task & calendar reminder emails", but the
           CC is applied by TaskReminderBuilder and the shared participant-mail seam ONLY.
           CalendarInviteEmailService resolves a SINGLE address (CalendarEmail ?? contact override
           ?? primary) and calls SendWithIcsAsync with no CC — there is no cc parameter on that
           method at all. So the calendar half of the promise was never kept, and the invite can
           even land in a THIRD mailbox the banner never mentioned. Say what is true, per mail
           family, and name the calendar inbox when it differs. *@
        @if (hasSecondary)
        {
            <p style="margin:0;"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128231;</span>
                <strong>Your task reminders reach two inboxes.</strong>
                Task reminders and the hub&rsquo;s other emails to you go to your primary
                <strong>@primary</strong> and are also copied to <strong>@secondary</strong>.
                <a asp-page="/Profile" asp-fragment="AlternateEmail" style="white-space:nowrap;">Change &rarr;</a>
            </p>
            @if (calendarDiffers)
            {
                <p style="margin:6px 0 0;">
                    <strong>Calendar invitations are different:</strong> they go to
                    <strong>@calendarInbox</strong> only &mdash; a calendar invite is sent to one
                    mailbox, not copied.
                </p>
            }
            else
            {
                <p style="margin:6px 0 0;">
                    <strong>Calendar invitations are different:</strong> they go to
                    <strong>@primary</strong> only &mdash; they are not copied to your alternative
                    address.
                </p>
            }
        }
        else
        {
            <p style="margin:0;"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128231;</span>
                <strong>Want your task reminders in another inbox too?</strong>
                Right now they only go to <strong>@primary</strong>.
                <a asp-page="/Profile" asp-fragment="AlternateEmail" style="white-space:nowrap;">Add an alternative email &rarr;</a>
                and we&rsquo;ll copy your task reminders there as well.
                @if (calendarDiffers)
                {
                    <text>Calendar invitations are sent to <strong>@calendarInbox</strong> and are
                    not affected by this setting.</text>
                }
                else
                {
                    <text>Calendar invitations go to one mailbox only and are not affected by this
                    setting.</text>
                }
            </p>
        }
    </div>
}
